    <string name="settings_help">Help</string>
    <string name="help_download_failed">What if a download fails?</string>
    <string name="help_download_failed_body">How to fix:

(1) Check the link — it must be a YouTube / Facebook / TikTok link.
(2) Private or region-locked videos cannot be downloaded — choose a public one.
(3) Check your connection — Wi-Fi or mobile data may be unstable.
(4) Open Settings → Engine → Update engine to update yt-dlp.
(5) Still stuck? Contact the owner (@TKA_MTC).</string>
    <string name="help_no_sound">No sound in the video?</string>
    <string name="help_no_sound_body">For video files — YouTube serves video and audio separately. MMTube merges them with FFmpeg, so play the file with MX Player, VLC or ExoPlayer.

For MP3 — audio tags are written automatically.

An audio codec error can happen occasionally — tap retry and try again.</string>
    <string name="help_slow_quality">Download quality looks low?</string>
    <string name="help_slow_quality_body">MMTube automatically picks the highest quality the source offers (4K/1440p/1080p). If it still looks low:

• The source video may only have a low-quality stream
• Some Facebook/TikTok videos are only 720p/1080p
• YouTube can restrict quality by region
• Older Android phones may decode slowly</string>
